 {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "10 – 11 August 1932"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/305"} "Olympic Park Swimming Stadium, Los Angeles, California"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/5010"} "12 from 7 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "With defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/49375"} "Zus Philipsen-Braun"] " languishing in a hospital bed, the attention of the swimming world was fixed upon two swimmers: the glamorous " [:a {:href "/athletes/51060"} "Eleanor Holm"] " of the USA, who held the world record, and the woman whose record Holm had broken, " [:a {:href "/athletes/45093"} "Bonnie Mealing"] ", from Woolloomooloo, Australia."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Holm attacked the field from the start of the final, and was still gaining on the field at the finish to head Mealing by two seconds. Eleanor Holm was one of the most glamorous and controversial female sporting figured of the 1930s. In 1933, she married the popular singer and bandleader Art Jarrett, and for a while combined her swimming with performances alongside her husband’s band.  Despite her marriage, she continued competing and qualified for the " [:a {:href "/editions/11/sports/SWM"} "1936 Berlin Olympics"] ", but her attempt to retain her title ended before she even reached European soil. Two days out of New York, she was invited to a party thrown in honor of the journalists travelling with the Olympic team. Holm was seen drinking champagne until the early hours and was warned by team officials about her conduct. The breaking point came when the ship was docked at Cherbourg. Holm spent the day at several champagne parties and was discovered on deck by the team chaperone the worse for drink, and accompanied by a man, at 10:30 in the evening. Returned to her cabin, she proceeded to shout obscenities out of the porthole. The chaperone then returned with the team doctor, who was unable to wake her and diagnosed her as being in a state of “acute alcoholism”. In the morning, Holm woke to the news that she had been removed from the Olympic team and, despite taking her case to USOC president " [:a {:href "/athletes/78168"} "Avery Brundage"] ", she would not compete in Berlin."] "\n\n" [:p {} "She did, however, report on the Games for the International News Agency, and was an honored guest of the German organizers. On her return to America, she turned professional, divorced Art Jarrett and soon married Billy Rose, in whose Aquacade spectaculars she would star. A brief dalliance with Hollywood saw her co-star with " [:a {:href "/athletes/78811"} "Glenn Morris"] " in " [:em {} "Tarzan’s Revenge"] ", but that was to be her only acting appearance. She hit the headlines one more time due to scandalous divorce proceedings with Billy Rose before settling to a third and longer lasting marriage."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51060"} "Eleanor Holm"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:18.3 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:19.4 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45093"} "Bonnie Mealing"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:21.6 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:21.3 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47005"} "Valerie Davies"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "